~ start
if Gs.day == 1
	=> meeting_1
else
	%3 => meeting
	%2 => nothing
=> END

~ meeting_1
do Gs._stop()
Narrator: You should meet your new colleagues
set Gs.event = "1_meeting"
do Gs._play()
=> END

~ meet01
do Gs._stop()
Director: We are late with the execution of the plan! Everyone speed up 1003 times!
secretary: But today is the first working day!
Analyst: If we start right now, we will overtake our competitors in just 152 years.
Deputy Director: Exactly! all for the shawarma!
Economist: 17 times a day?! It will bankrupt the...
accountant: At my expense!
The guard: I won't believe you!
the accountant: Damn! I forgot that I have no money!
Manager: And when is the salary?
Director: The ruble has fallen!
Richard: I see.
Director: Let's get to work!
do Gs._play()
=> END
~ meet02
do Gs._stop()
Richard: And where is my salary?
director: Where's my car?
Secretary: Where are my glasses?
Deputy Director: Where's the plaque?
Richard: So where's my salary?
director: First, tell me where my car is.
Secretary: No, first tell me where my glasses are.
Deputy Director: The most important question is, where is the plaque?
Richard: The plaque is under repair.
Director: Salary in Switzerland.
Secretary: The car is in Siberia.
Deputy Director: Gypsies have glasses.
do Gs._play()
=> END
~ meet03
do Gs._stop()
Security guard: The New Year is coming soon!
Director: No!
Richard: What's "no"?
Director: No one will get the award!
Guard: And why?
Deputy Director: Because we have only 4 million allocated for the implementation of the plan, and we cannot spend it on bonuses and salaries.
Analyst: 4 million?! Not 2?!
Secretary: 2 million?! Not a million?!
Economist: a million?! Not 500 thousand?!
manager: 500 thousand?! Not 200?!
Richard: Was money allocated for this?!
* And silence...*
do Gs._play()
=> END
~ meet04
do Gs._stop()
Director: Tomorrow is the New Year, and we need to take stock.
Analyst: We made 500 nail boxes in a year.
secretary: You can also now knock on the director's door.
Richard: * mentally* We should try it.
Economist: We have successfully completed the plan by 705.6 percent.
Manager: All the real estate in the area is now ours.
Security guard: Security has improved by 1234567,890 percent.
Director: Thank you, everyone's free!
Janitor: Yes, go to hell!
do Gs._play()
=> END
~ meet05
do Gs._stop()
Methodologist: I have developed a new methodology for selling our new product.
Richard: And what kind of product is it?
methodologist: I present to your attention a completely relevant product that will be sold to the last unit!
director: Don't Tom, introduce your bike already!
Employee: * drumming on the table with a shot *
methodologist: Devourer of air!
Director: ...
Richard: ...
secretary: ...
security guard: This is A MASTERPIECE!!!
manager: This is...
Richard: Unnecessary...
employee: Empty...
secretary: Outdated...
economist: Expensive...
accountant: Sophisticated...
director: Great idea! We're starting to release!
Janitor: Great! Get out of here, I need to wash up.
do Gs._play()
=> END
~ meet06
do Gs._stop()
Janitor: Where's the director?
Richard: How should I know?
Deputy director: He went to another city on business.
The guard: That's why we don't have a single penny in our office. I'll run to look for him!*
the methodologist runs away: The director is a bastard! He stole everything and left!
Secretary: You're a brute!  The last scum!  It's not enough to kill!
Manager: No one is allowed to leave the premises! If he comes back, we'll tie him up and hand him over!
Janitor: I'm going to kill this thing with my own hands!
analyst: I'll tear it up on the spot!
Accountant: I won't let you bury him!
Economist: I'll destroy him and scatter his ashes!
Director: * enters from the toilet * Guys, where's the money? Where's the guard? Why are you so angry?
Richard: A security guard? He's gone to look for you...
director: Why are you looking for me? I decided to go to the bathroom on the way ...
* Meanwhile, in the Maldives *
the guard: Well, at least I took a vacation for the first time in 75 years of service.
employee: That's right...
the guard: And where are you from here?
Employee: Got through as luggage.
do Gs._play()
=> END
~ meet07
do Gs._stop()
Director: I have a small announcement!
employee: What is it? Have the dinosaurs escaped again? Have the aliens stopped trading again? 
Director: Better!
Secretary: Did the President raise salaries? 
Director: No, it's not! Even better!
Methodologist: Has Malakhov retired?
director: Even better!
Richard: Have the roads been built properly?
Director: No, not that well. It's time to give you your salary.
* Long pause *
Economist: Excuse me?
Director: It's time to pay your salary. Come one at a time.
Employee: *hesitantly approaches* What's my salary?
Economist: Like $150.
Director: * with obvious reluctance, he hands the employee a wad of money* They're yours. Next!
Employee: * departs *
Manager: * approaches* I remember! My salary is $200.
Director: I won't give it to you, you remember. Next!
Methodologist: You can pay...
manager: It's not fair! I honestly worked for 4 years without a salary, without days off and without delays! Give me a salary.
The guard: * hits the manager on the head and drags the body out the door * Let him breathe.
The methodologist: So I can have a salary, please.
Director: Okay, here's your $200. * holds out money* Next!
The methodologist: * departs* Thank you...
Analyst: *suitable*Give me my salary!
Director: * gives him a dryer* Next!
accountant: Major!
Analyst: * hides the dryer and walks away *
Accountant: * fits* And my salary.
Director: Your $350. * Gives the money back *
accountant: * walks away, quietly * It won't be enough.
Secretary: *suitable* And I need to, too.
Director: Okay, your $500. * Hands over the money *
the secretary: * departs *
the deputy director: I have already received my $1300.
Security guard: You have already given me a salary of 2 million.
Janitor: How much?! I only have $100.
Director: Everyone who has received a salary, go to work.
*Everyone except Richard and the director leave*
Director: Why are you sitting there?
Richard: I'm waiting for my 3 drying sessions.
Director: It's expensive. Maybe 2.3 drying?
Richard: No, 3 drying sessions.
Director: 2.5!
Richard: 2.9!
director: 2.65!
Richard: 2.8!
Director: Agreed! *Provides 3 drying methods*
do Gs._play()
=> END
~ meet08
do Gs._stop()
Director: A plan?
Analyst: Yes!
director: Money?
economist: Yes!
director: Salary?
accountant: Not issued!
director: Sauna?
manager: Heated!
director: Drinks?
Methodologist: Ordered and on the way!
director: Cake?
Employee: In the fridge, what's under lock and key!
director: Music?
janitor: Set up!
director: Neighbors?
Security guard: We moved out a couple of weeks ago!
Richard: And what's going on?
Secretary: The impulse is dead!/ st: Go your own way.
Richard: *leaves*
the deputy director: Call him in half an hour.
* after half an hour*
Richard: Where are you taking me? Zach...
Everyone: Happy birthday!!!
do Gs._play()
=> END


~ meeting
do Gs._stop()
Narrator: You need go to leaving room
set Gs.event = "meeting"
do Gs._play()
=> END

~ nothing
do Gs._stop()
Narrator: Today nothing to do
set Gs.event = ""
do Gs._play()
=> END

~ end_meet
Narrator: That's the end of the meeting, and the assignment for today is on your screen.
do Gs._play()
=> END